  "_source": "ORC-96. Expected values computed with Python decimal with 120 significant digits (far more than the cent needs) and rounded half up (away from zero) to the cent, independently of the app code. installments: French amortisation q = P·r/(1−(1+r)^−n), r = rate/1200, rate 0 → P/n (same rule as card_installments.json). monthlyInterest: capital·rate/1200. recurringMonthly: amount·timesPerYear/(12·every), timesPerYear = 52 (week), 12 (month), 1 (year). projection: monthly·Σ g^k for k = 1…months, g = (1 + rate/100)^(1/12) (each contribution at the start of its month). The large principals and amounts are cases where the old Double code was one cent off; 600 at 1 %, 999 every 2 weeks, 5 every 2 months, 18 a year and 3 over 3 months are exact half cents.",
